On 2009-01-09, David Damerell <damerell@chiark.greenend.org.uk> wrote:
> Quoting  Marc Hartstein  <marcmagus@gmail.com>:
>>It's a lance which never breaks, instead of breaking <0.05% of the
>>time.
>
> Mmm. Fair point that the non-artifact lance breaking rate is very low
> given the utility of jousting - but those very low odds apply only once
> you have maxed luck.

Actually, all you need is positive luck.

The difference between Luck 1 and Luck 13 is more or less irrelevant.
(In fact, 13 is slightly *more* likely to break, because rnl is
weird.)  Luck 0 is about 0.4% breaking, and it increases significantly
as luck gets more negative.

See the rnl calculator at http://tinyurl.com/9kpmkg
- you're looking at the bottom line, where rnl(50) == 49.
(http://klozoff.ms11.net/cgi-bin/nethack-rnl-calculator.pl)

I was wrong above, though; the chance of the lance breaking when you
have positive luck is <0.01% per hit.  (Only 1/5 of hits are eligible
for breaking.)

See also uhitm.c line 1153, or the footnote at
http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Lance


